{
  "_README": [
    "Revenue as filed at Companies House, read from the scanned accounts and",
    "checked by arithmetic: revenue minus cost of sales must equal gross profit,",
    "or revenue plus other income minus operating costs must equal operating",
    "profit. Every figure below passed that check against the filed page.",
    "Source PDFs are in sources/chains/<slug>/. Page numbers are in",
    "sources/chains/ocr_results.json.",
    "",
    "Figures are net of VAT, because UK turnover always is. That is the whole",
    "reason the VAT numbers in 13_vat_model.py have to be modelled."
  ],
  "_discontinuities": [
    "COSTA: the reporting entity and basis both change. To Feb 2019 these are",
    "consolidated group accounts under Whitbread ownership. Coca-Cola acquired",
    "Costa in January 2019 and the year end moved to December, producing a",
    "ten-month transition period to 31 December 2019. From 2020 the filing is",
    "Costa Limited's own income statement, not a consolidation. Do NOT read the",
    "2018-19 and 2020-24 figures as one continuous series.",
    "",
    "GAIL'S: the group parent changes. To February 2021 the filer is Bread",
    "Holdings Limited (07570780). From August 2021 the group sits under Grain",
    "Topco Limited (13572366, SIC 64209 holding company), whose first period is",
    "a stub of about six months to February 2022 and is therefore excluded from",
    "the annual series rather than annualised.",
    "",
    "PRET: the filer is Pret A Manger (Europe) Limited, the main UK and European",
    "trading entity, not the worldwide group. FY2024 is a 53-week year, so",
    "per-week comparison is needed before calling FY2025 a decline."
  ],
